IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `P7-gates`

-- P7-database: Article 71 of the EU Artificial Intelligence Act (Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744):
-- the EU database for high-risk AI systems listed in Annex III. Article 71 is in the provision group `General` (Chapter VIII applies from 2 August 2026)
-- and the Omnibus did not change it (no marker line inside it).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Seams: S1 (the route by which the AI system is high-risk, from the core), S6 (registration under Article 49).
-- Names that come from other parts' provisions (Articles 6(3), 6(4), 49, Annex VIII, Annex IX) are plain facts asked as BOOLEAN inputs.
-- The text is the Publications Office consolidation of 27.7.2026, a rendering with no legal effect.

§ `Article 71: the EU database`

-- src:1107 | 1. The Commission shall, in collaboration with the Member States, set up and maintain an EU database containing information referred to in paragraphs 2 and 3 of this Article concerning high-risk AI systems referred to in Article 6(2) which are registered in accordance with Articles 49 and 60 and AI systems that are not considered as high-risk pursuant to Article 6(3) and which are registered in accordance with Article 6(4) and Article 49. When setting the functional specifications of such database, the Commission shall consult the relevant experts, and when updating the functional specifications of such database, the Commission shall consult the Board.
@ref Art 71(1) first sentence, the duty (src:1107)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the Commission sets up an EU database in collaboration with the Member States` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission maintains the EU database in collaboration with the Member States` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 71(1) the Commission has set up and maintained an EU database in collaboration with the Member States` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 57 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter VI and Chapter VIII (group General) apply from the date Art 113 gives
        OTHERWISE JUST (`the Commission sets up an EU database in collaboration with the Member States` AND `the Commission maintains the EU database in collaboration with the Member States`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Commission shall, in collaboration with the Member States, set up and maintain an EU database containing information referred to in paragraphs 2 and 3 of this Article"

-- src:1107 | 1. The Commission shall, in collaboration with the Member States, set up and maintain an EU database containing information referred to in paragraphs 2 and 3 of this Article concerning high-risk AI systems referred to in Article 6(2) which are registered in accordance with Articles 49 and 60 and AI systems that are not considered as high-risk pursuant to Article 6(3) and which are registered in accordance with Article 6(4) and Article 49. When setting the functional specifications of such database, the Commission shall consult the relevant experts, and when updating the functional specifications of such database, the Commission shall consult the Board.
@ref Art 71(1) first sentence (the systems the database holds information about) (src:1107)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the AI system has been registered under Article 49` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the testing of the AI system in real world conditions has been registered in accordance with Article 60` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system is not considered as high-risk pursuant to Article 6(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system has been registered in accordance with Article 6(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 71(1) the EU database contains information concerning the AI system` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 57 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter VI and Chapter VIII (group General) apply from the date Art 113 gives
        IF `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` EQUALS `Route Article 6(2) and Annex III` AND (`the AI system has been registered under Article 49` OR `the testing of the AI system in real world conditions has been registered in accordance with Article 60`) THEN JUST TRUE  -- "high-risk AI systems referred to in Article 6(2) which are registered in accordance with Articles 49 and 60" (the two registrations are read as alternatives: fork F-71-1)
        IF `the AI system is not considered as high-risk pursuant to Article 6(3)` AND `the AI system has been registered in accordance with Article 6(4)` AND `the AI system has been registered under Article 49` THEN JUST TRUE  -- "AI systems that are not considered as high-risk pursuant to Article 6(3) and which are registered in accordance with Article 6(4) and Article 49"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the paragraph says what the database is to contain and does not say that it may contain nothing else

-- src:1107 | 1. The Commission shall, in collaboration with the Member States, set up and maintain an EU database containing information referred to in paragraphs 2 and 3 of this Article concerning high-risk AI systems referred to in Article 6(2) which are registered in accordance with Articles 49 and 60 and AI systems that are not considered as high-risk pursuant to Article 6(3) and which are registered in accordance with Article 6(4) and Article 49. When setting the functional specifications of such database, the Commission shall consult the relevant experts, and when updating the functional specifications of such database, the Commission shall consult the Board.
@ref Art 71(1) second sentence, setting the functional specifications (src:1107)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the Commission is setting the functional specifications of the database` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission consults the relevant experts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 71(1) the Commission has consulted the relevant experts when setting the functional specifications of the database` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 57 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter VI and Chapter VIII (group General) apply from the date Art 113 gives
        IF NOT (`the Commission is setting the functional specifications of the database`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "When setting the functional specifications of such database"
        OTHERWISE JUST (`the Commission consults the relevant experts`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When setting the functional specifications of such database, the Commission shall consult the relevant experts"

-- src:1107 | 1. The Commission shall, in collaboration with the Member States, set up and maintain an EU database containing information referred to in paragraphs 2 and 3 of this Article concerning high-risk AI systems referred to in Article 6(2) which are registered in accordance with Articles 49 and 60 and AI systems that are not considered as high-risk pursuant to Article 6(3) and which are registered in accordance with Article 6(4) and Article 49. When setting the functional specifications of such database, the Commission shall consult the relevant experts, and when updating the functional specifications of such database, the Commission shall consult the Board.
@ref Art 71(1) second sentence, updating the functional specifications (src:1107)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the Commission is updating the functional specifications of the database` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission consults the Board` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 71(1) the Commission has consulted the Board when updating the functional specifications of the database` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 57 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter VI and Chapter VIII (group General) apply from the date Art 113 gives
        IF NOT (`the Commission is updating the functional specifications of the database`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "when updating the functional specifications of such database"
        OTHERWISE JUST (`the Commission consults the Board`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "and when updating the functional specifications of such database, the Commission shall consult the Board"

-- src:1108 | 2. The data listed in Sections A and B of Annex VIII shall be entered into the EU database by the provider or, where applicable, by the authorised representative.
@ref Art 71(2) (src:1108)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the provider enters the data listed in Sections A and B of Annex VIII into the EU database` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authorised representative enters the data listed in Sections A and B of Annex VIII into the EU database` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 71(2) the data listed in Sections A and B of Annex VIII have been entered into the EU database` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 57 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter VI and Chapter VIII (group General) apply from the date Art 113 gives
        OTHERWISE JUST (`the provider enters the data listed in Sections A and B of Annex VIII into the EU database` OR `the authorised representative enters the data listed in Sections A and B of Annex VIII into the EU database`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The data listed in Sections A and B of Annex VIII shall be entered into the EU database by the provider or, where applicable, by the authorised representative"

-- src:1109 | 3. The data listed in Section C of Annex VIII shall be entered into the EU database by the deployer who is, or who acts on behalf of, a public authority, agency or body, in accordance with Article 49(3) and (4).
@ref Art 71(3) (src:1109)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the deployer is, or acts on behalf of, a public authority, agency or body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deployer enters the data listed in Section C of Annex VIII into the EU database in accordance with Article 49(3) and (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 71(3) the data listed in Section C of Annex VIII have been entered into the EU database by the deployer` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 57 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter VI and Chapter VIII (group General) apply from the date Art 113 gives
        IF NOT (`the deployer is, or acts on behalf of, a public authority, agency or body`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the deployer who is, or who acts on behalf of, a public authority, agency or body"
        OTHERWISE JUST (`the deployer enters the data listed in Section C of Annex VIII into the EU database in accordance with Article 49(3) and (4)`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The data listed in Section C of Annex VIII shall be entered into the EU database by the deployer who is, or who acts on behalf of, a public authority, agency or body, in accordance with Article 49(3) and (4)"

-- src:1110 | 4. With the exception of the section referred to in Article 49(4) and Article 60(4), point (c), the information contained in the EU database registered in accordance with Article 49 shall be accessible and publicly available in a user-friendly manner. The information should be easily navigable and machine-readable. The information registered in accordance with Article 60 shall be accessible only to market surveillance authorities and the Commission, unless the prospective provider or provider has given consent for also making the information accessible the public.
@ref Art 71(4) first sentence (src:1110)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the information is registered in accordance with Article 49` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is not in the section referred to in Article 49(4) and Article 60(4), point (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is accessible` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is publicly available` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is accessible and publicly available in a user-friendly manner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 71(4) the information registered in accordance with Article 49 is accessible and publicly available in a user-friendly manner` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 57 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter VI and Chapter VIII (group General) apply from the date Art 113 gives
        IF NOT (`the information is registered in accordance with Article 49` AND `the information is not in the section referred to in Article 49(4) and Article 60(4), point (c)`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "With the exception of the section referred to in Article 49(4) and Article 60(4), point (c), the information contained in the EU database registered in accordance with Article 49"
        OTHERWISE JUST (`the information is accessible` AND `the information is publicly available` AND `the information is accessible and publicly available in a user-friendly manner`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the information contained in the EU database registered in accordance with Article 49 shall be accessible and publicly available in a user-friendly manner"

-- src:1110 | 4. With the exception of the section referred to in Article 49(4) and Article 60(4), point (c), the information contained in the EU database registered in accordance with Article 49 shall be accessible and publicly available in a user-friendly manner. The information should be easily navigable and machine-readable. The information registered in accordance with Article 60 shall be accessible only to market surveillance authorities and the Commission, unless the prospective provider or provider has given consent for also making the information accessible the public.
@ref Art 71(4) second sentence (src:1110)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the information is easily navigable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is machine-readable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 71(4) the information is easily navigable and machine-readable` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 57 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter VI and Chapter VIII (group General) apply from the date Art 113 gives
        IF `the information is easily navigable` AND `the information is machine-readable` THEN JUST TRUE  -- the grant: "The information should be easily navigable and machine-readable"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "should" is a recommendation; information that is not navigable or machine-readable is not told in the text that it may not be

-- src:1110 | 4. With the exception of the section referred to in Article 49(4) and Article 60(4), point (c), the information contained in the EU database registered in accordance with Article 49 shall be accessible and publicly available in a user-friendly manner. The information should be easily navigable and machine-readable. The information registered in accordance with Article 60 shall be accessible only to market surveillance authorities and the Commission, unless the prospective provider or provider has given consent for also making the information accessible the public.
@ref Art 71(4) third sentence (who may access the information registered in accordance with Article 60) (src:1110)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the person seeking access is a market surveillance authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person seeking access is the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prospective provider or provider has given consent for also making the information accessible to the public` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 71(4) the person may access the information registered in accordance with Article 60` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 57 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter VI and Chapter VIII (group General) apply from the date Art 113 gives
        OTHERWISE JUST (`the person seeking access is a market surveillance authority` OR `the person seeking access is the Commission` OR `the prospective provider or provider has given consent for also making the information accessible to the public`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be accessible only to market surveillance authorities and the Commission, unless the prospective provider or provider has given consent for also making the information accessible the public"

-- src:1111 | 5. The EU database shall contain personal data only in so far as necessary for collecting and processing information in accordance with this Regulation. That information shall include the names and contact details of natural persons who are responsible for registering the system and have the legal authority to represent the provider or the deployer, as applicable.
@ref Art 71(5) first sentence (src:1111)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the personal data are necessary for collecting and processing information in accordance with this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 71(5) the EU database contains personal data only in so far as necessary for collecting and processing information in accordance with this Regulation` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 57 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter VI and Chapter VIII (group General) apply from the date Art 113 gives
        OTHERWISE JUST (`the personal data are necessary for collecting and processing information in accordance with this Regulation`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The EU database shall contain personal data only in so far as necessary for collecting and processing information in accordance with this Regulation"

-- src:1111 | 5. The EU database shall contain personal data only in so far as necessary for collecting and processing information in accordance with this Regulation. That information shall include the names and contact details of natural persons who are responsible for registering the system and have the legal authority to represent the provider or the deployer, as applicable.
@ref Art 71(5) second sentence (src:1111)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
